: none of them boots; the question: what are the options that were used to 
: build that kernel? is 2.0.32 OK or should I look for some patches?

you have to do:

cd /some/where/NOT/usr/src (include problems?)
tar zxvf linux-2.0.XX.tar.gz
cd linux
change "ARCH = i386" for "ARCH = alpha" at top of Makefile
make config (not menuconfig/xconfig)
make boot (you will get an arch/alpha/boot/vmlinux.gz for booting
           with aboot, there is not MILO for mikasa yet)

For me it is very bad (kernel oopses at boot time) option
CONFIG_ALPHA_SRM_SETUP (Use SRM PCI setup), but my box is an
1000A 5/333 (noritake-primo).

I don't know if you must/should use alpha patches from
gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/DEC/Linux-Alpha/Kernels... I have to use
them because noritake is not supported yet by normal linux kernel.
I suppose somebody owning a mikasa can give you some advice...

I think you will find usefull http://www.azstarnet.com/~axplinux/,
included .../~axplinux/srm.html.

